// `for` goes over a range, a list or a map's entries (REFERENCE §6.5). Sets come later
// (Q37), and anything else is a type mismatch. Its pattern must match every element, as a `let` pattern does (OPEN_QUESTIONS
// P5), so a variant or a literal in it is E0318, and a tuple pattern needs a tuple of its
// length. A pattern that is one name binds it whatever its case, as in a `let`, so a
// wrongly cased one is E0204 and its uses report nothing more. A loop variable can't be
// assigned. A collection that nothing gives a type is E0312, and one with an error reports
// nothing more, in the loop or its body.
